From b878ba13a0fb2c0dfbc5fa26eeeff86d28e9527e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:16:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] NetBpfLoad: neutralize the 25Q4/26Q4 kernel-version
 aborts too

The original 'NetBpfLoader: Support no bpf usecase' patch removed the
hard return from every kernel-version gate that existed at the time
(S/T's 4.9, U's 4.14, V's 4.19, 25Q2's 5.4). Upstream has since added
two more gates for 25Q4 (5.10) and 26Q4 (5.15) that didn't exist when
that patch was written, and their 'return 7;' is still live.

Since this is a 26Q2 build, isAtLeast25Q4 is true, and this kernel is
3.10, so doLoad() would hit this return before ever reaching the
execve() handoff into 'netbpfload done' that sets bpf.progs_loaded.
netbpfload.rc's 'wait_for_prop bpf.progs_loaded 1' would then block
forever, hanging boot before netd ever starts -- a much worse failure
mode than the reboot-loop the original patch guarded against.

Audited the rest of this function and the other no-bpf-usecase patches
(system/bpf's Loader.cpp/bpfloader.rs, netd's Controllers.cpp,
BpfNetMaps.java's initBpfMaps()) for the same pattern; this was the
only live one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Idc2dd28e9993ebfd810f8a765d5c17060a34a5eb
---
 bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp b/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
index a50cbb9943..6e87f05de9 100644
--- a/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
+++ b/bpf/loader/NetBpfLoad.cpp
@@ -1573,13 +1573,11 @@ static int doLoad(char** argv, char * const envp[]) {
     // see also: //system/netd/tests/kernel_test.cpp TestKernel510
     if (isAtLeast25Q4 && !isAtLeastKernelVersion(5, 10)) {
         ALOGE("Android 25Q4 requires kernel 5.10.");
-        return 7;
     }
 
     // 26Q4 bumps the kernel requirement up to 5.15
     if (isAtLeast26Q4 && !isAtLeastKernelVersion(5, 15)) {
         ALOGE("Android 26Q4 requires kernel 5.15.");
-        return 7;
     }
 
     // Technically already required by U, but only enforce on V+
